# Offline InfoSys Lookup (MSHC)

## Search Priority

**Always offline first, online only as fallback.**

1. `twincat_infosys_mshc_search` (offline, structured, fast)
2. Only if offline returns 0 results → `twincat3-infosys-lookup` skill (web)

## How to Search

Tool-call shapes, modes (`auto` / `fulltext` / `symbol` / `title`), optional filters (`library`, `parent`), formatting (`format="json"|"markdown"`), and `twincat_infosys_mshc_read` usage → skill `twincat3-infosys-mshc` (`skills/twincat3-infosys-mshc/SKILL.md`).

| Situation | Mode / approach |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Known type name | default `auto` (`auto_read=true` → one call often enough) |
| Method/Property with known parent | pass `parent="FB_..."` or `library="Tc3_..."` to disambiguate |
| Concept known, name unknown | `fulltext` (BM25; all query words) |
| Partial name | prefix in fulltext (e.g. `FB_Json*`) |
| Exact phrase | quote the phrase in fulltext |
| Only IEC symbols (FB, ST, E, I, F, M, P) | `symbol` |
| Token-efficient prompt output | default (`format="markdown"`) |

## Search Strategy for Unknown Types

1. Try the most specific query first (exact name if known)
2. If disambiguation is needed (e.g. `Reset`, `AddJsonMember`), provide `parent="FB_..."` or `library="..."`
3. If 0 results: broaden to description keywords in fulltext mode
4. If 0 results: try prefix search with type prefix (`FB_*`, `ST_*`, `E_*`, `M_*`, `P_*`)
5. If still 0 results: fall back to online InfoSys (`twincat3-infosys-lookup` skill)

## Performance & Token Efficiency

- Title/symbol search: <1ms (in-memory)
- BM25 fulltext: 1-3ms (SQLite FTS5 Schema v2)
- Page reads: <10ms via persistent ZipFile handle caching
- Token budget: Structured output without body bloat (<500 tokens), saves >65% context
- First-ever search: ~13s (builds FTS5 DB in %TEMP%/twincat-mcp-infosys-mshc)
- Subsequent server restarts: ~0.2s (loads from cached DB)
